message.content:
Progesterone capsules in measured doses, put up for retail sale, are classified in heading 3004 as medicaments containing hormones. Subheading 3004.39 covers medicaments containing hormones or other products of heading 2937, not containing antibiotics. Progesterone is a steroid hormone of heading 2937, and the 3004.39 subheading is "Other."

The HTSUS statistical suffix for 3004.39.00 is 3004.39.0000, and I believe that is the 10-digit number. Under 3004.32 (corticosteroid hormones), progesterone is not a corticosteroid, so it falls in 3004.39. There is also a 3004.39.00 breakout in the US schedule, so 3004.39.0000 should be correct.

